adverseReactions:
Testosterone gel, 1% is contraindicated in men with carcinoma of the breast or known or suspected carcinoma of the prostate [see Warnings and Precautions (

                           5.1

                        ), Adverse Reactions (

                           6.1

                        ), and Nonclinical Toxicology (

                           13.1

                        )]. 
                      Testosterone gel, 1% is contraindicated in women who are pregnant. Testosterone gel, 1% can cause virilization of the female fetus when administered to a pregnant woman. Pregnant women need to be aware of the potential for transfer of testosterone from men treated with testosterone gel, 1%. If a pregnant woman is exposed to testosterone gel, 1%, she should be apprised of the potential hazard to the fetus [see Warnings and Precautions (
                              5.2
                           ) and Use in Specific Populations (
                              8.1
                           )].
